-- title:
--   Corollary 5.4 — ARC(S) reaches −λ_min(Q_kᵀB_kQ_k) ≤ ε within O(ε^(−3)) iterations
-- statement:
--   Let $f:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb R$ and consider a run of ARC(S) (Algorithm 4.1) with parameters $\gamma_2\ge\gamma_1>1$, $1>\eta_2\ge\eta_1>0$, $\sigma_0>0$ and $\kappa_\theta\in(0,1)$. Assume:
--
--   1. **AF.3**: $f\in C^2(\mathbb R^n)$, with gradient $g$ and Hessian $H$;
--   2. **AF.4**: $\|g(x)-g(y)\|\le\kappa_H\|x-y\|$ for all $x,y$ in an open convex set $X$ containing all iterates $x_k$, for some $\kappa_H\ge1$;
--   3. **AF.6**: $\|H(x)-H(y)\|\le L\|x-y\|$ for all $x,y$, with $L>0$;
--   4. **AM.4**: $\|(H(x_k)-B_k)s_k\|\le C\|s_k\|^2$ for all $k$, with $C>0$;
--   5. $f(x_k)\ge f_{\rm low}$ for all $k$, and $\sigma_k\ge\sigma_{\min}>0$ for all $k$ (2.11);
--   6. $m_k(s_k)<f(x_k)$ for all $k$ (2.6);
--   7. each $s_k$ is a global minimizer of $m_k$ over a subspace $\mathcal L_k$ spanned by the orthonormal columns of a matrix $Q_k$.
--
--   Write $\lambda_k=\lambda_{\min}(Q_k^\top B_kQ_k)$ and set
--
--   $$L_0=\max\big(\sigma_0,\tfrac32\gamma_2(C+L)\big),\quad \alpha_{\rm curv}=\frac{\sigma_{\min}}{6L_0^3},\quad \kappa_{\rm curv}=\frac{f(x_0)-f_{\rm low}}{\eta_1\alpha_{\rm curv}},$$
--
--   $$\kappa^u_S=\frac{\log(L_0/\sigma_{\min})}{\log\gamma_1},\qquad \kappa^t_{\rm curv}=(1+\kappa^u_S)\kappa_{\rm curv}+\kappa^u_S .$$
--
--   Then for every $\epsilon>0$:
--
--   1. the successful iterations with negative curvature $-\lambda_k>\epsilon$ (5.24) are finitely many, at most $L^s_2=\lceil\kappa_{\rm curv}\epsilon^{-3}\rceil$ (5.25);
--   2. some iterate $l$ has $-\lambda_l\le\epsilon$, so the first iterate $l_2$ with $-\lambda_{l_2+1}\le\epsilon$ exists; and if $-\lambda_k>\epsilon$ for all $k\le j$, then at most $L^s_2$ of the iterations $0,\dots,j$ are successful; so $l_2$ is generated within $L^s_2$ successful iterations, i.e. gradient evaluations;
--   3. if moreover $\epsilon\le1$, every such $j$ satisfies
--
--   $$j\ \le\ \left\lceil\kappa^t_{\rm curv}\,\epsilon^{-3}\right\rceil =: L_2, \qquad (5.27)$$
--
--   so ARC(S) needs at most $L_2$ iterations (and function evaluations) to reach $-\lambda_{l_2+1}\le\epsilon$.
--
--   The bound is of order $\epsilon^{-3}$, the order Nesterov and Polyak proved for exact global minimization of the cubic model with the exact Hessian; here the model uses an approximate Hessian and is minimized only over subspaces.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\lambda_{\min}(Q_k^\top B_kQ_k)$ is the Rayleigh-quotient minimum of $B_k$ over unit vectors of $\mathcal L_k$ (definition `lamMin`), which equals the leftmost eigenvalue of $Q_k^\top B_kQ_k$ for every orthonormal basis matrix $Q_k$; for $\mathcal L_k=\{0\}$ Lean's empty infimum is $0$, so (5.24) fails there. (2.6) is assumed for all $k$, following the paper's convention that it holds "unless the ARC(S) algorithm terminates" (p. 4 and the last paragraph of §4, p. 12); runs that terminate are therefore outside the statement. "Assuming (5.24) holds at $k=0$ … takes at most $L$ iterations" is stated as: every $j$ with (5.24) at all $k\le j$ satisfies the bound, which never presumes that the first failure index exists; its existence, which the page asserts ("takes at most $L^s_2$ successful iterations … to generate … $l_2$"), is the separate conjunct $\exists l,\ -\lambda_l\le\epsilon$ of part 2. AF.4 is kept although this proof does not use it.
-- source:
--   Cartis, Gould & Toint, Adaptive cubic regularisation methods for unconstrained optimization. Part II, preprint rev. 15 Sep 2009 (UNamur), p. 16, Corollary 5.4, (5.24)–(5.27); p. 14, (5.18)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AdaptiveCubic_SecondOrder_IsARCSRun
import Definitions.Def_AdaptiveCubic_SecondOrder_lamMin

open scoped RealInnerProductSpace

namespace AdaptiveCubic.SecondOrder

/-- Corollary 5.4, p. 16 (Cartis, Gould & Toint, *Adaptive cubic regularisation methods for
unconstrained optimization. Part II*, preprint rev. 15 Sep 2009).

Let AF.3–AF.4, AF.6 and AM.4 hold. Let {f(x_k)} be bounded below by f_low and σ_k, as in (2.11).
Let s_k in ARC(S) be the global minimizer of m_k(s) over a subspace L_k that is generated by the
columns of an orthogonal matrix Q_k and let λ_min(Q_kᵀ B_k Q_k) denote the leftmost eigenvalue of
Q_kᵀ B_k Q_k. Then, given any ε > 0, the total number of successful iterations with negative
curvature −λ_min(Q_kᵀ B_k Q_k) > ε (5.24) that occur when applying the ARC(S) algorithm is at most
L^s_2 := ⌈κ_curv ε^{−3}⌉ (5.25), where κ_curv := (f(x_0) − f_low)/(η_1 α_curv) and
α_curv := σ_min/(6L_0³) (5.26), with σ_min and L_0 defined in (2.11) and (5.4), respectively.
Assuming that (5.24) holds at k = 0, the ARC(S) algorithm takes at most L^s_2 successful iterations
or equivalently, gradient evaluations, to generate a (first) iterate, say l_2, with
−λ_min(Q_{l_2+1}ᵀ B_{l_2+1} Q_{l_2+1}) ≤ ε. Furthermore, when ε ≤ 1, we have
l_2 ≤ ⌈κ^t_curv ε^{−3}⌉ := L_2 (5.27), and so the ARC(S) algorithm takes at most L_2 (successful and
unsuccessful) iterations, and function evaluations, to generate −λ_min(Q_{l_2+1}ᵀ B_{l_2+1} Q_{l_2+1}) ≤ ε,
where κ^t_curv := (1 + κ^u_S)κ_curv + κ^u_S and κ^u_S is defined in (5.18).

Formalization: (i) the set of successful `k` with (5.24) is finite with at most `L^s_2` elements;
(ii) some iterate `l` has `−λ_min(Q_lᵀB_lQ_l) ≤ ε`, so the first `l₂` with (5.24) failing at `l₂ + 1`
exists, and every `j` with (5.24) at all `k ≤ j` has `|S_j| ≤ L^s_2`, so `l₂` is reached within
`L^s_2` successful iterations; (iii) if `ε ≤ 1`, every
such `j` satisfies `j ≤ L_2`. `λ_min(Q_kᵀB_kQ_k)` is `lamMin (B k) (Lsub k)`;
(2.6) for all `k` is a hypothesis (p. 12, last paragraph of §4). -/
theorem corollary_5_4 {n : ℕ} (f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ) (γ₁ γ₂ η₁ η₂ κθ : ℝ)
    (x s : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) (σ : ℕ → ℝ)
    (B : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) →L[ℝ] EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))
    (hrun : IsARCSRun f γ₁ γ₂ η₁ η₂ κθ x s σ B)
    (hAF3 : ContDiff ℝ 2 f)
    (X : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) (hXo : IsOpen X) (hXc : Convex ℝ X)
    (hxX : ∀ k, x k ∈ X) (κH : ℝ) (hκH : 1 ≤ κH)
    (hAF4 : ∀ y ∈ X, ∀ z ∈ X, ‖gradient f y - gradient f z‖ ≤ κH * ‖y - z‖)
    (L : ℝ) (hL : 0 < L)
    (hAF6 : ∀ y z, ‖fderiv ℝ (gradient f) y - fderiv ℝ (gradient f) z‖ ≤ L * ‖y - z‖)
    (C : ℝ) (hC : 0 < C)
    (hAM4 : ∀ k, ‖(fderiv ℝ (gradient f) (x k) - B k) (s k)‖ ≤ C * ‖s k‖ ^ 2)
    (flow : ℝ) (hflow : ∀ k, flow ≤ f (x k))
    (σmin : ℝ) (hσmin : 0 < σmin) (h211 : ∀ k, σmin ≤ σ k)
    (h26 : ∀ k, AdaptiveCubic.Cauchy.model f (B k) (σ k) (x k) (s k) < f (x k))
    (Lsub : ℕ → Submodule ℝ (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))) (hsL : ∀ k, s k ∈ Lsub k)
    (hmin : ∀ k, ∀ t ∈ Lsub k,
      AdaptiveCubic.Cauchy.model f (B k) (σ k) (x k) (s k) ≤ AdaptiveCubic.Cauchy.model f (B k) (σ k) (x k) t)
    (ε : ℝ) (hε : 0 < ε) :
    let L₀ := max (σ 0) (3 / 2 * γ₂ * (C + L))
    let αcurv := σmin / (6 * L₀ ^ 3)
    let κcurv := (f (x 0) - flow) / (η₁ * αcurv)
    let κuS := Real.log (L₀ / σmin) / Real.log γ₁
    let κtcurv := (1 + κuS) * κcurv + κuS
    (({k | η₁ ≤ AdaptiveCubic.Cauchy.rho f (B k) (σ k) (x k) (s k) ∧ ε < -lamMin (B k) (Lsub k)}).Finite ∧
      (({k | η₁ ≤ AdaptiveCubic.Cauchy.rho f (B k) (σ k) (x k) (s k) ∧ ε < -lamMin (B k) (Lsub k)}).ncard : ℤ) ≤
        ⌈κcurv * ε ^ (-3 : ℤ)⌉) ∧
    ((∃ l : ℕ, -lamMin (B l) (Lsub l) ≤ ε) ∧
      ∀ j : ℕ, (∀ k ≤ j, ε < -lamMin (B k) (Lsub k)) →
      (((Finset.range (j + 1)).filter
        (fun k => η₁ ≤ AdaptiveCubic.Cauchy.rho f (B k) (σ k) (x k) (s k))).card : ℤ) ≤ ⌈κcurv * ε ^ (-3 : ℤ)⌉) ∧
    (ε ≤ 1 → ∀ j : ℕ, (∀ k ≤ j, ε < -lamMin (B k) (Lsub k)) →
      (j : ℤ) ≤ ⌈κtcurv * ε ^ (-3 : ℤ)⌉) := by sorry

end AdaptiveCubic.SecondOrder
